    },
    {
      "id": "ct4-04-nqueens-algorithm-t1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 51,
      "y": 275.0,
      "width": 738,
      "height": 360.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1701,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1702,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Read n; fill board[n][n] with 0s.\n2. In isSafe(row, col), check the same column above:\n   inspect board[i][col] for i = 0..row−1; a 1 means false.\n3. Scan upper-right from i = row−1, j = col+1.\n   While i ≥ 0 and j < n, check each cell; a 1 means false.\n   Otherwise move up-right: i ← i−1, j ← j+1.\n4. Scan upper-left from i = row−1, j = col−1.\n   While i ≥ 0 and j ≥ 0, check each cell; a 1 means false.\n   Otherwise move up-left: i ← i−1, j ← j−1.\n   If all three scans are clear, return true.\n5. In solve(row), if row == n, return true.\n6. Try each col = 0..n−1 in this row.\n   If isSafe(row, col) is false, try the next column.\n   Otherwise place queen: board[row][col] ← 1.\n   Call solve(row + 1); if true, return true.\n   If it fails, undo: board[row][col] ← 0; continue.\n7. If no column works, return false.\n8. Call solve(0); print board if true, else \"No solution\".",
      "originalText": "1. Read n; fill board[n][n] with 0s.\n2. In isSafe(row, col), check the same column above:\n   inspect board[i][col] for i = 0..row−1; a 1 means false.\n3. Scan upper-right from i = row−1, j = col+1.\n   While i ≥ 0 and j < n, check each cell; a 1 means false.\n   Otherwise move up-right: i ← i−1, j ← j+1.\n4. Scan upper-left from i = row−1, j = col−1.\n   While i ≥ 0 and j ≥ 0, check each cell; a 1 means false.\n   Otherwise move up-left: i ← i−1, j ← j−1.\n   If all three scans are clear, return true.\n5. In solve(row), if row == n, return true.\n6. Try each col = 0..n−1 in this row.\n   If isSafe(row, col) is false, try the next column.\n   Otherwise place queen: board[row][col] ← 1.\n   Call solve(row + 1); if true, return true.\n   If it fails, undo: board[row][col] ← 0; continue.\n7. If no column works, return false.\n8. Call solve(0); print board if true, else \"No solution\".",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "ct4-04-nqueens-algorithm-n1",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 16
    },
